    "reason": "[ev-653d842efc60] describes a new beta, finalizer-based cleanup that removes Kyverno-managed webhook configurations on uninstall, and says it is not yet the default. It does not name a Helm value, flag or feature gate that turns the feature on, which would be the subject, and it does not say which installations use it, which would decide applicability. For those details it only links to the uninstallation docs (\"Clean up webhooks\"), which are not shown here. The rendered diffs are about other changes (apiCall.default CRD fields [ev-9348cb2d7f00] and the Service appProtocol [ev-bcf9822c2eb4]), so they don't fill the gap. We still need that uninstallation docs section or the chart value or flag that enables the finalizer cleanup.",
